    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d556">

                <pb facs="0619" n="539" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg539"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Raikes to Mr.
                            Hill</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Bar
                            Harbor</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1902-07-30"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 30,
                    1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note No. 2502, of the 25th instant, in which you are good enough to
                    forward a copy of a dispatch addressed to you by the United States consul at
                    Guadeloupe, giving a general account of the acts performed by him for British
                    subjects on the occasion of the late disaster at Martinique, in the absence of
                    any British representative in that island.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to express to you my sincere thanks for this interesting
                    communication, a copy of which I have forwarded to His Majesty’s principal
                    secretary of state for foreign affairs.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Arthur S. Raikes.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
